## 1. Mermaid diagram source

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    R["INTERMEDIATE TRACE EXERCISE<br/>Illustrative models only<br/>Assume the starting node emits a faulty output<br/>Affected means receiving that output"]

    subgraph CENTRAL["Illustrative centralized coordination"]
        C0["Coordinator<br/>faulty start<br/>assigns model tasks and combines model results"]
        C1["Agent 1<br/>affected"]
        C2["Agent 2<br/>affected"]
        C3["Agent 3<br/>affected"]
        C0 -->|task marked faulty| C1
        C0 -->|task marked faulty| C2
        C0 -->|task marked faulty| C3
        C1 -->|result returns| C0
        C2 -->|result returns| C0
        C3 -->|result returns| C0
    end

    subgraph SEQUENTIAL["Illustrative sequential handoff"]
        S1["Agent A<br/>faulty start"]
        S2["Agent B<br/>affected"]
        S3["Agent C<br/>affected"]
        S1 -->|output handed forward| S2
        S2 -->|output handed forward| S3
    end

    subgraph PARALLEL["Illustrative parallel fan-out and convergence"]
        P0["Dispatcher<br/>faulty start<br/>assigns model tasks"]
        P1["Agent X<br/>affected"]
        P2["Agent Y<br/>affected"]
        P3["Agent Z<br/>affected"]
        P4["Collector<br/>affected<br/>combines model results"]
        P0 -->|task marked faulty| P1
        P0 -->|task marked faulty| P2
        P0 -->|task marked faulty| P3
        P1 -->|result converges| P4
        P2 -->|result converges| P4
        P3 -->|result converges| P4
    end

    subgraph PEER["Illustrative peer-to-peer interaction"]
        A["Peer A<br/>faulty start"]
        B["Peer B<br/>affected"]
        C["Peer C<br/>affected"]
        D["Peer D<br/>affected"]
        A -->|output sent| B
        A -->|output sent| C
        B -->|output sent| D
        C -->|output sent| D
        D -->|feedback sent| A
    end

    R -->|apply assumption| C0
    R -->|apply assumption| S1
    R -->|apply assumption| P0
    R -->|apply assumption| A
```

